4. SELF-REVIEW the diff against the issue's Acceptance Criteria. Remove anything that is not strictly required. Stop if you have drifted into a Non-Goal.
5. STOP after committing on the feature branch. Do NOT push and do NOT open a pull request — automated simplify and review passes run over your diff next, and a dedicated finalize step opens the draft PR (linking the issue with "Closes #42") once they are done. Leave the branch checked out with your commits on it.
